{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head c61b5c4b78ffd6ad8a00cc392fcd5335c68337bd (tree b5e3a512deab7a627b39505bd345014be631db64), BO1-W1 step 1 with the documents corrected, on published c02f76a0. The verdict binds the structural implementation promise b8d7bd6c (request 55b67149) and signs all six path artifacts, with the 19bfa371 artifact first. It answers my change request aaeb0842 and carries my review of the source, test and gate forward. It authorizes no deploy. The planner lands and deploys.\n\n## One of my four asks was wrong\nIn aaeb0842 I asked to remove `dap-commons` from the `DEMO_START_CONFIG` row of the Workers lookup in `docs/security/settings.md`. The builder kept it, and the builder is right. The lookup is generated from the code-read inventory, and `scripts/security-settings.mjs` fails with \"undocumented setting read\" when a deployment's code reads a setting that its row does not list. The shared `fetch.ts` reads `DEMO_START_CONFIG` for every room Worker, including Commons, and the Commons file now leaves the setting unset. So the row must list `dap-commons`, and the new sentence in settings.md says why. The machine inventory and the generated lookup are byte-identical to 73d4056e (the lookup block hashes equal at both heads).\n\n## The correction\n`git diff 73d4056e c61b5c4b` changes four files:\n- **entry-points.md.** \"Its three register fields hold `unplanned`\" becomes \"Both register fields hold `unplanned`\".\n- **settings.md.** The Commons paragraph says \"both register fields\" and \"has no Commons Start setting\". The false \"retained metadata\" sentence is gone. A new sentence says the Workers column lists every deployment whose code can read a setting, even when its config omits it, and that Commons omits `DEMO_START_CONFIG`, so its shared reader sees the setting as absent. That is accurate and it explains the one row that looks wrong.\n- **trust-boundaries.md.** The sentence about a checked-in `DEMO_START_CONFIG` now says the configuration has none, so the Page offers no Start link. It keeps the order link and \"bind only the two operational register fields\".\n- **The structure note.** One sentence now says the review head adds the note and updates the security documents, and that the gated configuration and test match the review head byte-for-byte.\n\n## Evidence\n- **Source stands.** `git diff --name-only 8a9bcfc6 c61b5c4b -- apps packages scripts` is empty, so the source and test are those of the gated head 8a9bcfc6. The gate evidence I verified in aaeb0842 stands (`gate.txt` `e8185014…`, exit 0, 1,283.25 s, END c6acb343). docs/evidence-filing.md covers a documents-only successor.\n- **Artifacts.** The six filed artifacts equal the six changed paths (`git diff --no-renames --name-only c02f76a0 c61b5c4b`): the Worker config, the CLI test, the structure note and the three security documents. None is missing, extra or twice.\n- **Checks.** The merge into origin/main is clean with tree b5e3a512. `check-commit-messages` flags none of 3 commits, `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. The added lines carry no other project's name and no `/Users/` path.\n\n## Wake rate\nDocuments only on this delta, and configuration and a test below it. No alarm, retry or reschedule is added, so the wake floor and requests per room per hour are unchanged.\n\n## Architecture\nThe Commons Worker is closed while both register values are `unplanned`, and the four documents now say two fields, no Start setting, and why the lookup still lists it.\n\n## Security\nThe removed Start offer, the closed creation state and the test's pin grammar stand as in aaeb0842. The documents now match them.\n\n## Simplification\nNothing to remove.\n\n## Non-blocking\nThe note sentence \"The review head adds this note … The gated configuration and test match the review head byte-for-byte\" uses \"the review head\" for two things: the head under review (c61b5c4b) and, in the second sentence, the gated head (8a9bcfc6). Name the gated head's hash in the second sentence at the next edit.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:19bfa371c726b203b4542559d947a35c63c1544b","binding":"assigned","head":"c61b5c4b78ffd6ad8a00cc392fcd5335c68337bd","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4e655e3ad426ae6b4b47221a40737fec3ae85f2b\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b8d7bd6cc04987a5eaac496925c70f22abb2f36f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8fe5d75acd338a942dcfad140467558c23f1feb3","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}